@senpaiofsavage3072 their post season performance is making it to the National Championship game, Einstein. You’re talking about decades ago? College football teams are different year to year, even more so coach to coach, and even more so since NIL. Welcome to 2026. 

Furthermore, Notre Dame didn’t avoid a conference; the conferences avoided them. In particular, Notre Dame lobbied to enter the Big10 for years, yet Michigan ensured they never got in. Eventually the gave up and decided staying independent made more sense financially, as it does. It’s a huge blessing and they’re going to be one of the most dominant teams for decades because of it. Remember that whole NIL thing? I know the world is a lot different now and hard to understand, yet Notre Dame has a LOT of money. Get use to it. 

Lastly, the only series Notre Dame ever had to cancel was Michigan which their agreement with the ACC to play 6 games per season required a series to drop. I would love for that game to come back, yet it would require dropping another rivalry game, so it’s a tough spot. Either way, your representation of them canceling games because they’re “scared” is pathetic and sad. You don’t know much about anything to do with this.

